did see a Singleton on the Boid Spawner in Chapter 27, "Object-Oriented Think-
ing," we haven't used them yet in Part II of the book. A Singleton is a coding
pattern where only a single instance of a class will ever exist, and it should be
public. Here, we've modified the MissionDePolition.S Singleton to make it
private. This allows us to implement static public methods like SH2TB)IRED()
that can be called by any other class while not allowing access to any fields of
MissionDemolition by any other classes. Please see Appendix B, "Useful
Concepts," for more information on the Singleton pattern.
